## Project commands

Devbox provides one root interface across every selected component:

```sh
devbox run init
devbox run fmt
devbox run check
devbox run test
devbox run build
```

`fmt` updates formatting. `check`, `test`, and `build` are separate, non-deploying
validation stages used by the generated GitHub Actions workflows.
{% if frontend_playwright | default(false) or client_playwright | default(false) %}
After installing the configured Playwright browsers, run end-to-end tests separately:

```sh
devbox run test:e2e
```
{% endif %}

Pushing a `v*` tag runs validation and publishes a GitHub Release containing the
selected build artifacts. It does not deploy Workers, push container images, or
publish to an application store.
{% if 'backend' in components and 'fastapi' in backend_variants %}
## FastAPI backend

The independent Python service is in `backend/fastapi/`.

```sh
uv sync --project backend/fastapi
uv run --project backend/fastapi ruff check backend/fastapi
uv run --project backend/fastapi ruff format --check backend/fastapi
uv run --project backend/fastapi ty check backend/fastapi/app
uv run --project backend/fastapi pytest backend/fastapi
docker buildx build --output type=oci,dest=backend/fastapi/dist/fastapi-backend.tar backend/fastapi
```

The Docker build creates a local OCI-compatible image and does not publish it.
{% endif %}
{% if 'backend' in components and 'hono' in backend_variants %}
## Hono backend

The independent Cloudflare Worker service is in `backend/hono/`.

```sh
bun install --cwd backend/hono
bun run --cwd backend/hono check
bun run --cwd backend/hono test
bun run --cwd backend/hono build
```

The build command uses Wrangler's local `--dry-run` mode and writes the edge
artifact to `backend/hono/dist/`; it does not deploy remote resources.
{% endif %}
{% if 'client' in components %}
## Desktop client

The independent Tauri application is in `client/`.

```sh
bun install --cwd client
bun run --cwd client check
bun run --cwd client test
cargo fmt --manifest-path client/src-tauri/Cargo.toml --all -- --check
cargo check --manifest-path client/src-tauri/Cargo.toml --all-targets --all-features
cargo clippy --manifest-path client/src-tauri/Cargo.toml --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings
cargo test --manifest-path client/src-tauri/Cargo.toml --all-features
bun run --cwd client tauri build --bundles deb,appimage
```

The final command requires Linux WebKitGTK and related Tauri prerequisites and
emits AppImage and Debian bundles below `client/src-tauri/target/release/bundle/`.
macOS and Windows bundles require their respective native runners and are not
built by the generated workflows.
{% if client_playwright %}
Install Chromium with `bunx --cwd client playwright install chromium`, then run
`bun run --cwd client test:e2e`.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
